	That was probably a mistake. DSM of either type would've given
you the ability to cast spells without losing your AC, as well as MR or
reflection. Even if you wished for silver and traded it in for gray
later (I would've just wished for gray), having that nine-plus points of
spell-friendly AC early in the game is well worth having to burn another
wish late in the game (remember, you're guaranteed at least five if you
can clear the Castle). Unless I'm playing a monk, some sort of DSM is
practically always my first wish.

	Don't waste a wish on a ring of slow digestion. Unless you're
running a diet conduct, it's nowhere near worth it. There's far more
food in the dungeon than you should ever need. If you're having hunger
problems, it's because you're staying in one place and giving most of
your kills to your god. Get moving, get yourself access to all that food
in the dungeon below you, and start eating your kills yourself, and your
food problems will go away.

	My next step would be to PUT ON MAGIC RESISTANCE!, and then head
down the dungeon, explore down to Medusa's, bridge the lake, make
absolutely certain that I was wearing my amulet of reflection before
opening Medusa's door, and then continue on to clear the Castle and
retrieve the WoW. Then I'd make sure I had a blessed scroll of charging
(found, written, or wished, whatever it took) and I'd wish up some
blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail and whatever else I felt I really
needed, charging wand as necessary, and then I'd brush up on my sleep
spell and go take out the Cyclops. After that, clear Gehennom, make
final preparations, kill Rodney, do Invocation, grab Amulet, run to high
altar, ascend.

